member.summary:
Runtime control panel - the collapsible UI on the right edge of the scene that lets the operator tweak the hands without restarting the app or opening the Godot editor.
Hosts:
sliders for the control-hand movement timing (Frequency / HoldTime / RestTime);
a freeze toggle (calls );
a chirality toggle (currently disabled - both hands stay left);
a smoothing toggle + speed for the predicted hand ();
buttons to Load Config File (open a file dialog and point VHI at any TOML on disk) and Edit Config File (OS.ShellOpen the current config in the system text editor).
Collapsed by default; toggled with the > chevron on the right edge. No driver-mode toggle - that is set in the Inspector or over gRPC ().

Name of the optional LSL inlet that drives the control hand
            in . Resolved by name only;
            missing is fine - the inlet is simply skipped.
